{"step_index":95,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:37:26Z","thinking":"**Evaluating Current Task Scope**\n\nReviewing the provided constraints, current authority is limited to the local snapshot and reversible changes within this product. Live external actions or production mutations are explicitly outside this scope, preventing any direct impact on external systems or live data. Focus will be on analyzing the snapshot to determine ordinary, reversible objectives.\n\n\n**Analyzing Offer R7 Performance**\n\nThe Quiet Return (R7) offer, source `record-b7ab79e22e`, targeted US returning iOS annual subscribers with a 20% discount.  Initial positive metrics, documented in `record-da3a9e962e`, showed promise, but the offer was rolled back on 2026-07-21 due to unresolved refund escalations. Later, a mature ledger review, `record-802325ed36`, likely modified the interpretation of the early data. The dates of the observation window and the initial recorded data are unknown.\n\nThe decision is to review the complete record.\n\n\n**Analyzing R7 Offer Findings**\n\nObserved data from `record-b7ab79e22e` indicates R7 experienced a 6.2% net revenue decrease after refund adjustments despite unchanged trial starts; no price or eligibility changes justify repetition. The rollback on July 21st remains a relevant event, confirmed by data. The \"Quiet Return\" name was reused for a different cohort, as documented in `record-3965c8ff16`, targeting desktop monthly subscribers.\n\nFurther analysis shows \"Harbor\", source `record-dc92607ff3`, a plan picker for new US mobile accounts, had a short deployment window (August 10th - August 18th) documented through `record-eb44fddf46` and `record-4cd3618639`. This demonstrates another instance of offer experimentation, rollout, and rollback. The source `record-783bf16` is under consideration for additional insights.\n\n\n**Investigating Harbor Plan Picker Impact**\n\nInitial data from the \"H