y illustration colors. Because refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts (`brief.md`), cosmetic artwork changes do not justify repeating an economically negative offer. (A rece\n<truncated 12968 bytes>\nretired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md` | Deployed 2026-07-12; rolled back 2026-07-21 | Quiet Return R7 (US returning iOS annual) | 50% exposure July 13–19 *(year unstated)*; rolled back due to unresolved refund escalations. |\n162: | `record-da3a9e962e` | `history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md` | Recorded 2026-07-20 | Quiet Return R7 (July 13–19) | Initial funnel metric: trial starts +11%; net revenue immature. |\n163: | `record-802325ed36` | `history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md` | Recorded 2026-08-04 | Quiet Return R7 correction | Refund-adjusted net revenue was -6.2% below control; repeating R7 unjustified. |\n164: | `record-3965c8ff16` | `history/evidence/record-3965c8ff16.md` | Recorded 2026-09-06 | Quiet Return W3 name reuse | Desktop monthly cohort +4% net revenue; explicitly does not cover mobile R7. |\n165: | `record-dc92607ff3` | `history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md` | Deployed Aug 10; rolled back Aug 18 *(years unstated)* | Harbor H1 (New US mobile accounts) | Deployed Aug 10, rolled back Aug 18; initial -9% revenue report and permission reset bug. |\n166: | `record-783bf16383` | `history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md` | Recorded August 18 *(year unstated)* | Harbor H1 observation | Reported -9% revenue; double-counted resumed sessions; 7 of 12 sessions reset annual choice. |\n167: | `record-47eaba418e` | `history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md` | Recorded 2026-08-24 | Harbor H1 correction | Deduplicated revenue is +1.8% (inconclusive); reset bug confirmed real; neither loss nor win. |\n168: | `record-3c858d6a57` | `history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md` | Dated 2026-09-02 | Offer proposals (Quiet Return & Harbor H2) | Quiet Return only changed colors (same R7); Harbor H2 fixes reset bug (tested in QA record-0d1c74ca54). |\n169: | `record-0d1c74ca54` | Cited in `record-3c858d6a57.md` | Unknown *(prior to 2026-09-02)* | Harbor H2 QA | Confirmed absence of permission dialog reset across 18 test device runs. |\n170: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":101,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:38:00Z","content":"The dated recommendation for the revenue responsibility has been written to [/workspace/work/decision.md](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Recommendation\n\n* **Recommendation:** **Harbor (Variant H2)** deserves the next experiment on new mobile accounts. **Quiet Return (Variant R7)** should **not** be run.\n* **Why Quiet Return is Rejected:** The previous mobile deployment of Quiet Return R7 ([`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md)) initially showed +11% trial starts ([`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)), but mature ledger analysis accounting for refunds revealed net revenue was **-6.2% below control** ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). The refreshed design proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) changed only illustration colors while retaining the identical R7 discount and mobile checkout. Per [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts; superficial cosmetic changes do not justify re-testing an economically negative offer.\n* **Why Harbor H2 is Supported:** Harbor H1's ([`record-dc92607ff3`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md)) initial -9% revenue report was distorted by session double-counting and corrected to **+1.8% (inconclusive)** ([`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)). Furthermore, 7 of 12 reviewed sessions experienced a bug where the OS permission dialog reset the chosen annual plan ([`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)). The Harbor H2 proposal fixes this reset behavior, confirmed in QA across 18 device runs ([`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)), leaving the underlying revenue hypothesis viable and ready for an unconfounded test.\n* **Next Evidence Needed:** Pre-flight telemetry deduplication verification, in-flight production telemetry confirming selection retention across the permission dialog, controlled rollout receipts, and an observation window long enough to measure mature refund-adjusted net revenue.\n\nPlease inspect [/workspace/work/decision.md](file:///workspace/work/decision.md) for full action histories, source citations, date preservation details, and uncertainty analysis."}
